<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Daeng Chelak</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1745">1745</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Daeng Chelak was one of five <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bugis">Bugis</a> brothers from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sulawesi">Sulawesi</a> who won great influence in the Malay world in the early 18th century. He served as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yang-dipertuan-muda">Yang Dipertuan Muda</a>, or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a>, of the Johor-Riau Sultanate and fought on its behalf across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strait-of-malacca">Strait of Malacca</a>. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salehuddin-of-selangor">Raja Lumu</a> became the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> of Selangor, founding the dynasty that still reigns there.</p></div>
